  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant for the People Affected by the Typhoon Disaster in Viet Nam and Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the overall objective of saving lives and protecting populations severely affected by Typhoon Yagi while bolstering their capacity to recover, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is implementing interventions expected to benefit over 16,900 individuals. This includes the distribution of life-saving non-food items to 4,200 households (16,800 individuals), dissemination of public health messaging and rehabilitation of evacuation-related infrastructure to ensure safer conditions for 100 affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
